could still be in the cards once again  the name of the game is wait and see but  if there's one thing we know about lobo  it's that he never quits might take me a  week it might take me ten years but i'm  gonna bust out  dc nabbed an oscar winner for their  planned blackhawk film stephen spielberg  who has taken home three academy awards  will produce and likely direct a film  based on blackhawk the leader of an  international squadron of pilots who  take on the nazis during world war ii  the blackhawk character debuted in  1941's military comics number one and  was originally published by quality  comics before dc acquired it in 1956.  the character who was co-created by will  eisner bob powell and chuck quidera  headlined a number of best-selling  comics in the 1940s his world war ii  background makes him a great fit for  spielberg who earned an oscar for  directing the world war ii drama saving  private ryan spielberg is bringing on  indiana jones and the crystal skull and  jurassic park writer david kepp to pen  the script in 2022 four years after the  project got underway kep told collider  that while a script is written warner  brothers has yet to give the blackhawk  production a green light according to  the screenwriter there were a lot of  management changes at warner brothers so  i think we've just been kind of waiting  for that to settle down and for them to  decide what they want to do with their  dc universe  the dcu's current version of superman  may be up in the air but one project  warner brothers is reportedly high on is  a starring cinematic vehicle for his  cousin supergirl the character is  already enjoying a high profile thanks  to the success of her cw tv series and  the time seems right for the dc eu to  introduce another powerful female lead  actress sasha kaje who beat out hundreds  of other auditioners will be dceu's  supergirl kache's only major role to  date is on the young and the restless  but she'll make her debut as cara zorel  in the flash before taking to the skies  in supergirl little is known about this  in development project other than its  screenwriter oren uzil who penned the  cloverfield paradox the rumor mill has  suggested the project could be set in  the 1970s in an alternate timeline where  cara arrives on earth before her cousin  this would set the film version of the  character apart from her tv incarnation  uzil has been at work on the script  since august 2018 so more details are  sure to surface  dc is looking to bring a little magic  into its cinematic universe the studio  is aiming to put zatana zatara a  powerful magic user into her own feature  film considering some of the other  projects being floated around the dc  universe such as justice league dark  zetana's debut fits perfectly into dc's  current plans the project is very early  in development but one important detail  has been confirmed emerald finnell the  writer of the academy award-nominated  film promising young woman has been  tapped to write the screenplay in an  interview with empire fennell said she's  excited for the scales zatana gives her  to work with and she can't wait to write  something quite dark that's also big and  scary since it's so early we don't have  any casting information yet surrender  swan played zatanna in the cw show  smallville but since that series wrapped  up over a decade ago it seems unlikely  she would be cast as the lead of the new  film  birds of prey introduced us to quite the  crew of dc anti-heroes though it mainly  gave margot robbie's harley quinn a  chance to fly solo it also introduced us  to updated takes on black mask huntress  victor zazz and black canary the last  one apparently made a good impression as  actor journey smilet has been tapped to  reprise her role in her own solo film  wanna hear a secret  [Music]  while still very early in development we  do have an idea who's going to help  bring a black canary movie to life  smollett will be reuniting with  lovecraft country creator misha green  who's penning the script black canary is  also being produced by sue kroll of  crowling co entertainment who also  produced birds of prey the film is in  development for an hbo max release  suggesting it'll be smaller in scale  than the pillar dc eu movies involving  the justice league  fans of early 2000's animation might  remember the static shock series which  aired on kids wb for four seasons based  on the milestone comics character virgil  hawkins is a 14 year old boy who gains  electrical and magnetic powers after a  freak accident and becomes the superhero  static during the 2021 fan dome event a  static shock movie was confirmed to be  in development with randy mckinnon  pending the script reginald hudlund is  overseeing the relaunch of milestone  comics is also working behind the scenes  in addition michael b jordan's  production company outlier society is  helping to bring the film to life in  october 2020 jordan told the hollywood  reporter i'm proud to be a part of  building a new universe centered around  black superheroes our community deserves  that outlier society is committed to  bringing to life diverse comic book  content across all platforms and we are  excited to partner with reggie and  warner brothers on this initial step  dc is starting to dig deeper into their  bag of tricks for characters they want  to build films around and their latest  offbeat choice is our men there have  been multiple characters who've taken up  that mantle but they all center around a  chemical formula that grants the user  incredible abilities for one hour we've  actually seen several versions of our  man in the cw's arrowverse patrick j  adams played rex tyler the original hour  man on legends of tomorrow while lou  ferrigno jr played the character on star  girl cameron gelman played rex's son  rick tyler on star girl and took on the  our man mantle himself however it  remains to be seen what direction dc  will go with the hour man film the  screenplay is being tackled by gavin  james and neil widner chernin  entertainment which also developed the  most recent planet of the apes franchise  is producing the film alongside dc and  warner brothers  wonder woman is regarded as one of the  dceu's best efforts and director patty  jenkins says there are plenty more  stories to tell about diana's amazon  sisters dc is currently working on a  spin-off about these warrior women and  while the details are scarce jenkins has  said the spin-off will focus on events  that occur after diana leaves themsira  she also said the story would help  bridge the gap between wonder woman 1984  and diana's third film that seems to  indicate that the spin-off will be  released before the in development  wonder woman 3. jenkins will not be  directing this spin-off but she is  involved in the film's creative  development as a producer we expect  other amazons to reappear but details  remain tightly wrapped up at this point  unlike wonder woman 1984's hbo max  release wonder woman 3 will have a  traditional theatrical release and is  expected to be a concluding film to the  trilogy during 2021's fandom writer  director patty jenkins also revealed  that original wonder woman linda carter  will be returning as amazonian warrior  asteria that said it could still be a  long while before we get to finish the  story of diana prince jenkins and star  gal gadot are working together on the  historical drama cleopatra and jenkins  has been tapped to direct star wars  rogue squadron which is scheduled to  come out in christmas 2023. gadot is  attached to about a half dozen other  projects as well in other words it's  going to be a while but we'll eventually  get to see another wonder woman movie on  the big screen
 

